# AGENTS.md

## Project

`<<armonia:project.name>>` is governed by Armonìa. Read `.armonia/project.yaml` before making
changes and use `armonia inspect` to discover components and capabilities.

## Canonical commands

- `armonia validate`: validate the manifest and active policy profile.
- `armonia plan`: preview generated-file changes.
- `armonia run test`: execute the declared test capability.
- `armonia run build`: execute the declared build capability.

## Boundaries

- Do not edit files reported as `managed` in `.armonia/lock.yaml`.
- Do not run `armonia apply --force` without reviewing every conflict.
- Do not add secrets to the repository, manifest, workflow, or agent instructions.
- Keep technology-specific commands in the component capability map.
- Record durable architecture decisions in `docs/decisions/`.

## Definition of done

The relevant tests pass, `armonia validate` reports no errors, documentation reflects the
change, and generated-file drift is resolved.
